{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A Psalm of Asaph. El</b> — the sense is powerful to execute judgment, therefore Elohim." "And the sense of YHWH — that He is an eternal dweller without change." "<b>And He calls the earth</b> — He calls the inhabitants of the earth, from the rising of the sun to its setting; such is the inhabited world, even though not all of the earth is inhabited, rather less than a quarter by clear proofs."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:21.703482421Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}